# No code comments

Do not write code comments. Docs are the only source of truth. A rule,
product lock, decision, "dev only" gate, history or reason goes in the doc
that owns the surface (sume-com: `docs/`, `AGENTS.md`), never in a comment.
Do not encode a product lock in a comment, and do not write "see the docs"
comments.

A comment you find is not a lock. If it states a rule the code still follows
and the docs lack it, write the rule into the owning doc and delete the
comment. Tests must not assert on comment text or use comments as anchors.

Keep only what a tool reads: shebangs, SPDX / license headers, and compiler
or linter directives (`@ts-expect-error`, `@ts-ignore`, `eslint-disable`,
`prettier-ignore`, `/* raw-colour: … */`, …), with no narrative after them.

Source of truth: `~/.cstack/src/docs/CODE-COMMENTS.md`.
